{"name":"Searchlight","hex":"#eff0bf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Searchlight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Clark County, Nevada, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Searchlight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Searchlight","blocks":[{"text":"A searchlight is an apparatus that combines an extremely bright source with a mirrored parabolic reflector to project a powerful beam of light of approximately parallel rays in a particular direction. It is usually constructed so that it can be swiveled about. The most common element used in modern searchlights is xenon (Xe). However, rare-earth elements such as lanthanum (La) and cerium (Ce) are used in phosphors to improve light quality in some specialized searchlights."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_the_United_Kingdom_1939_-_1945_H36315.jpg/330px-The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_the_United_Kingdom_1939_-_1945_H36315.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Searchlight"},{"title":"Searchlight (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Searchlight is a British magazine, founded in 1975 by Gerry Gable and Maurice Ludmer, which publishes exposés about racism, antisemitism and fascism in the United Kingdom and elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Searchlight_magazine_logo.png/330px-Searchlight_magazine_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Searchlight_(magazine)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Attaque_nocturne.jpg/500px-Attaque_nocturne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Attaque_nocturne.jpg/500px-Attaque_nocturne.jpg?utm_sou